INT. CAR WASH TUNNEL - NIGHT

Brushes idle. Soap drips. Three cars' worth of silence.

KAVEH RAZMI (40s, wet suit jacket) crouches behind a spinning mitter curtain, gun low. He is breathing hard.

Across the bay, MARISOL "SOL" DUARTE (30s, mechanic's coveralls) holds a wrench like a club.

A speaker crackles overhead, then goes dead.

KAVEH
Sol. Put it down.

SOL
You first, Kav.

They speak at once.

KAVEH
I didn't take it.

SOL ^
You didn't take it.

Sol laughs once. Short. Dead.

SOL (CONT'D)
(muttering)
Four years.

A third silhouette steps through the exit light. TOBIAS WREN (60s, dry, immaculate raincoat).

TOBIAS
Evening, both.

Kaveh's gun drifts toward Tobias. Sol's wrench stays on Kaveh.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
Nobody here's leaving angry. Which is the point.

He sets a thin black case on the wet floor and slides it forward.

Sol drops the wrench. It rings. Kaveh lowers the gun.
